BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: Family Plot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T150000
UID:6a359beac7d3cd5800618189@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of Family plot movie.\nA phony psychic and con man are a conniving couple 
 who plot to swindle an old lady out of her fortune by telling her they can
  find her long-lost nephew. In the process\, their lives become intertwine
 d with a larcenous jewel merchant and his beautiful girlfriend who have an
  affinity for kidnapping. Filled with plot twists from beginning to end\, 
 the final film from the Master of Suspense is a fitting finale to his illu
 strious career.\nRated PG. 2hrs.\nEnglish Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard 
 of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a359beac7d3cd5800618189
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: The Brutalist
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T164500
UID:6a359ad44407827f8aa60c02@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of The Brutalist movie.\nEscaping post-war Europe\, visionary architect La
 szlo Toth arrives in America to rebuild his life\, his work\, and his marr
 iage to his wife Erzsb̌et after being forced apart during wartime by shif
 ting borders and regimes. On his own in a strange new country\, Laszlo set
 tles in Pennsylvania\, where the wealthy and prominent industrialist Harri
 son Lee Van Buren recognizes his talent for building. But power and legacy
  come at a heavy cost...\nRated R. 3hr 35mins.\nEnglish Subtitles for the 
 Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a359ad44407827f8aa60c02
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: I was a stranger
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T150000
UID:6a3598ff4407827f8aa60bc4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of I was a stranger movie.\nA doctor\, a soldier\, a smuggler\, a father\
 , and a captain. Each one on their own journey. Their paths cross in a des
 perate pursuit of safety and belonging. Set across four countries and insp
 ired by real stories from the frontlines of the refugee crisis\, this swee
 ping drama captures the heartbreak\, danger\, and fragile beauty of those 
 who dare to start over when the world gives them nothing.\nRated PG. 1hr 4
 3 mins.\nEnglish Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when ava
 ilable.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3598ff4407827f8aa60bc4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: Pike River
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T151500
UID:6a3597e7f56bd86e00b7d133@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of Pike River movie.\nThe incredible true story of two women whose friends
 hip empowered them to fight for justice after the Pike River Mine Tragedy 
 took the lives of 29 men underground.\nRated PG. 2hr 11mins.\nEnglish Subt
 itles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) when available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3597e7f56bd86e00b7d133
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
