BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T160000
UID:69e14c242866a5b488490b3c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film.  Ingredient lists will
  be available upon request.\nBig Bang\nScientists explore the birth of the
  universe\, from the Big Bang through the cosmic “Dark Ages\,” using s
 tunning space-telescope imagery to reveal how the first galaxies and stars
  formed. Scientists also investigate what may have happened in the tiniest
  fraction of a second after the universe began\, bringing us closer than e
 ver to understanding our cosmic origins. Closed Captions. 55 minutes.2021
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e14c242866a5b488490b3c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Runnymede Film Club Presents: Bonjour Tristesse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T200000
UID:6a5bc7c77b79214226a97ddd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a monthly film screening of\nBonjour Tristesse\n(2
 024\, Rated R)\n.\nEnglish and French spoken with English subtitles.\nAt t
 he height of summer\, 18-year-old Cecile is relaxing by the French seaside
  with her father and falling in love with her new boyfriend. The arrival o
 f her late mother's enigmatic friend turns her world upside down.\nDrop-in
 . No registration required.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5bc7c77b79214226a97ddd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
