BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Life Skills for Seniors: Online Health
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T153000
UID:6a61241a7b79214226aa74fd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is for people who have basic internet skills and 
 want to learn how to find trustworthy health information online. Learn to 
 evaluate websites for quality\, reliability and safety by looking at four 
 major areas of consideration before using any online health site. Find out
  the best types of organizations for providing high-quality information a
 nd provide a list of recommended sites. Resource handout provided.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a61241a7b79214226aa74fd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
