DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T140000
UID:6966a42d48a98474cec448dc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come and join our adult and senior's social as we engage in va
 rious activities\, games and crafts. Relax\, have fun\, and learn somethin
 g new while connecting with new friends. This programs runs on alternate T
 uesdays.
LOCATION:Woodview Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6966a42d48a98474cec448dc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artists in the Library: Animate with 16mm film
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T160000
UID:6a3d4ba6c7d3cd580062bffd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for one-of-a-kind workshop where you'll animate by han
 d on 16mm film to create your own short stop-motion piece. Participants wi
 ll be taught an array of direct animation techniques to scratch\, paint\, 
 draw\, on a film strip. Community viewing on Saturday November 14th\, 2-4 
 pm.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d4ba6c7d3cd580062bffd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talk About Books
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261014T150000
UID:6a3c4ed6f3bd131b675fd6af@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Looking for your next great read? Enjoy some refreshments\, le
 arn about some fabulous books from a library staff member\, and share what
  you've been reading. A fun way to discover new authors and titles!
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c4ed6f3bd131b675fd6af
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Humbermede Neighbourhood Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T194500
UID:6966a7f9c719ac98c336d066@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Humbermede Neighbourhood Community meeting allows neighbou
 rs to come together and discuss or learn about things happening in the com
 munity. Join the conversation\, connect with your neighbourhood community
  groups (e.g. Engage416 representative)\, accessing free resources and ha
 ve your voice heard regarding your concerns\, be part of the solution.
LOCATION:Woodview Park
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6966a7f9c719ac98c336d066
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260930T170000
UID:69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Board & Card Games
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260805T153000
UID:698676d57d180d0d4832d2e9@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in.\nBring your friends or make new ones while playing bo
 ard or card games. We’ve got the classics including Chess\, Checkers\, M
 onopoly\, Scrabble and more\n!
LOCATION:Richview\, 2nd floor Room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/698676d57d180d0d4832d2e9
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
