BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 4: Use Google Search
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260801T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260801T104500
UID:6a3d727b0e851028002d2c96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on using Google's filters and tools for absolute begin
 ners with little computer experience.\nIn this session you will:\nUse Goog
 le search tools more effectively to find websites\, images\, and news site
 s\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to use more advance
 d search engine features at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: Computers for B
 eginners 1\, 2 & 3 or basic mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills\nForma
 t: Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Second Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d727b0e851028002d2c96
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Housing Help
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260909T170000
UID:69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Drop in and work one-on-one with staff from The Housing Help C
 entre (THHC) to determine your housing needs\, connect you to other govern
 ment services\, and to match you with landlords across the city. THHC work
 s with both individuals and families in the City of Toronto to find and ma
 intain affordable\, safe housing.\nThe Housing Help Centre can be contacte
 d at 416-285-8070 or at shhc.ca.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Front Entrance
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69c1d0455a2d780f42c48ab2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
