BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T153000
UID:6a6129ea4523092f0031e28c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to use Gmail\, Google's free web-based email service.\nI
 n this sixth session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, rea
 d\, reply\, forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam and
  junk mail work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic 
 understanding of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and mana
 ge your own free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisites
 : Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demo
 nstrations.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Riverdale\, Program Room 1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6129ea4523092f0031e28c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
