BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indigenous Medicine Workshop: Cedar Salve
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260916T150000
UID:6a580ca8e9de6536001bfb85@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, participants will learn about the significa
 nce of Cedar from an Indigenous perspective Participants will also make
  a cedar salve. All supplies will be provided.\nThe program will be cappe
 d at the first 15 participants.\nTanya Gluvakov is a mixed Mohawk woman fr
 om Toronto with family and "roots" from Six Nations of the Grand River in 
 Oshweken\, Ontario. The founder of Roots and Raven\, Tanya is a herbalist\
 , a mom\, a teacher\, and auntie\, who teaches several workshops about med
 icines from the land and how connecting with them helps us find our way. S
 he also leads several projects that bring the resurgence of medicines and 
 accessibility to urban communities\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
