BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260828T120000
UID:6a56acc7c7e02e3d00692791@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.\nRegistration is required for this class and be
 gins August 14th\, 2026 at 12:30pm.\nNote: Your spot will not be guarantee
 d after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Not
 ice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pu
 blic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registrati
 on\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your
  information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\,
  416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a56acc7c7e02e3d00692791
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Word Basics 4: Formatting Reports and Long Documents
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T193000
UID:6a29dc50c7d3cd58005f769d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Practice your Microsoft Word skills when working with long doc
 uments.\nIn this class\, you will:\nUse Styles to effectively format\, str
 ucture and navigate your document\nCreate a Table of Contents\nUse Page an
 d Section breaks\nInsert Page Numbers and Footnotes\nInsert Web and docume
 nt links\nLearn about Microsoft Word's Accessibility features\nUpon comple
 tion of this class\, you will be able to format long documents\, such as b
 ooks\, reports\, and essays.\nPrerequisites:  Word Basics 1\, 2 & 3\, or e
 quivalent skills. Keyboarding and mouse skills are required.\nFormat: Hand
 s-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29dc50c7d3cd58005f769d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
