BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Romance Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260903T200000
UID:6a6a7d83f4e5db3d00c53c4e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Romance Book Club\, where love stories take cen
 ter stage and every page promises a new adventure of the heart. Whether yo
 u're into slow burns\, second chances\, or enemies-to-lovers\, there's som
 ething here for every kind of romantic. Come read\, swoon\, and share your
  favorite moments with fellow book lovers.\nBrentwood's Romance Book Club 
 title for Thursday September 3 is\nOur Perfect Storm\nby Carley Fortune.\
 nLimited copies will be available in branch for pick up starting August 6.
 \nPlease note that this book club is for individuals 18+.\nDrop in\, no re
 gistration required.\nOur Perfect Storm\nNote: At this meeting we will be
  voting on Brentwood's October Romance Book Club title.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a7d83f4e5db3d00c53c4e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Retirement Planning & Living
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T153000
UID:6a00cd39c7d3cd5800584d1c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:It's never too late to start thinking about investing! Managin
 g your finances to maximize your retirement years is the goal of retiremen
 t planning. Your retirement strategy should strike a balance between your 
 financial realities\, requirements and wants.\nThis presentation will cove
 r how to plan for retirement\, sources of retirement income and how to pro
 tect yourself from scams\, frauds and financial abuse.\nPresented by Canad
 ian Investment Regulatory Organization (CIRO)\, a national self-regulatory
  organization that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers a
 nd trading activity on Canada’s debt and equity marketplaces.
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a00cd39c7d3cd5800584d1c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
