BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Surviving Dementia Care: The Realities of Family Caregiving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T150000
UID:6a626ecff213992f00c682d1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This author talk will address the experiences of families who 
 are caring for a loved one who is living with dementia\, including the var
 ious points of stress\, as well as the various points of joy\, and ways in
  which caregivers learn to survive the experience. Major topics include un
 derstanding the diagnosis\, communicating with the loved one\, choosing an
  assisted living facility\, and using music and the arts as a means of con
 nection.\nPresented by Grant Campbell\, author of "\nSurviving Dementia Ca
 re\n: The Realities of Family Caregiving" (University of Toronto Press\, 
 2026).\nThe author will have copies of the book available for purchase and
  signing.
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a626ecff213992f00c682d1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
