DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T150000
UID:6a347954f56bd86e00b7ad6f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This book club is for readers who enjoy reading various types 
 of mysteries. Meetings will be held every\nthird Thursday\nof each month.\
 nOur goal is to have fun and travel the reading journey together.\nWe will
  be covering the following 4 books on the following dates:\nDeath in Focus
 \nby Anne Perry\n(September 17th)\nThe Mystery Writer\nby Sulari Gentill\n
 (October 15th)\nThe Hanging Girl\nby Jussi Adler-Olsen\n(November 19th)\nP
 oirot's Christmas\nby Agatha Christie\n(December 17th)\nNOTE\n: Contact u
 s three weeks prior the next meeting if you require a\nlarge print\ncopy\,
  if available.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, 3rd floor\, Discussion Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a347954f56bd86e00b7ad6f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
