BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mount Pleasant Cemetery History (evening presentation)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T193000
UID:6a3c23260e851028002cec18@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Sunnyside Historic Society Presents stories from the crypt
 !\nWhat is the connection between a survivor of the Titanic\, a world clas
 s pianist\, and a prime minister? T\nhey were all buried at Mount Pleasant
  Cemetery.\nJoin us for a combination of story-telling\, pictures\, and sh
 ort skits - on the history of Mount Pleasant Cemetery and the souls burie
 d there.\nNote: This program will run twice on the same day\, from 2-3:30p
 m and 6-7:30pm\, both being the same presentation. Please sign up for a ti
 me that suits you best.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c23260e851028002cec18
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
