UID:6a0762a143b41b3d0066bfaf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them. Yo
 u’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing na
 tive habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested 
 in urban ecology.\nThe last half hour will be to answer questions and have
  a group discussion.\nDrop-in\, no registration required\nThis program is 
 part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends o
 f Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0762a143b41b3d0066bfaf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moving Stories: A Movement Class for Older Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261019T113000
UID:6a554b12f213992f00c3f847@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this series\, participants will be introduced to the world 
 of art and creative storytelling through movement and music. These activit
 ies have been proven to improve circulation and joint mobility\, promote m
 ental stimulation\, improve posture and coordination\, and build strength 
 and balance. No previous movement experience is required. Each class build
 s upon the previous\, so participants are encouraged to attend each week.\
 nThis program is intended for\nolder adults\n.\nMoving Stories is brought 
 to you by tiger princess dance projects.\nMoving Stories is generously sup
 ported by the Canada Council for the Arts\, Ontario Arts Council & Toront
 o Arts Council.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information 
 on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public L
 ibraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will on
 ly be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Q
 uestions about how the library handles your information can be directed to
  Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Stree
 t\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Pape/Danforth\, Second floor program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a554b12f213992f00c3f847
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
