DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260914T143000
UID:6a5e86d4c7e02e3d006a7945@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on the following Monday afternoons to discuss books i
 n a friendly and social atmosphere: September 14th\, October 19th\, Novemb
 er 9th\, and December 14th.\nThis month we will be reading and discussing\
 nFoster\nby Claire Keegan.\nFoster\nby Claire Keegan is a moving and beaut
 ifully written novella about a young girl sent to live with relatives in r
 ural Ireland for the summer. In the warmth and care of her foster family\,
  she begins to thrive\, but an unspoken secret lingers beneath the surface
 . A poignant story of childhood\, belonging\, loss\, and love\,\nFoster\ni
 s an internationally acclaimed modern classic.\nParticipants can borrow a 
 copy of the book from the Woodside Square branch upon registration.\nInfor
 mation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collec
 ted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, section
 s 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event a
 nd program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the
