BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Senior’s Club: Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T150000
UID:6a5e56d6daaaf4f51a205f9b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 women and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a fragil
 ity fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Osteopor
 osis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your risk o
 f osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWhat you
  need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fracturing a
  bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical activ
 ity Fall prevention\nJoin us in July for a special summer edition of the 
 Senior's Club!\nThis month: Hands on Dinosaur Fossils & Ancient Life\nCom
 e in for an opportunity to handle\, examine up close and discuss nine rea
 l and replica fossils in this fascinating hands-on workshop. Participants 
 will be entertained and educated\, not just about the fossils themselves\,
  but the palaeontological aspects that underpin them. Concepts include: ev
 olution\, fossilization\, ‘The Tree of Life’ (phylogeny) and — of co
 urse — dinosaurs!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Cliffcrest
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a5e56d6daaaf4f51a205f9b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Life Skills: Online Travel
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260824T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260824T153000
UID:6a59135a9943bdf31e9f5457@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For people who have basic internet skills\, time and resources
  to pursue travel\, but want to learn about the online tools that can make
  it more affordable\, informed and flexible.  We will cover major transpor
 tation and accommodation websites and provide tips about booking online sa
 fely and securely.  With these skills you can design a personalized vacati
 on based on your schedule\, budget and varied interests!  Resource handout
  provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
  used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questi
 ons about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answ
 erline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, T
 oronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Learning Centre\, 1st Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a59135a9943bdf31e9f5457
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
