BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What If: Using the 6 Senses to Launch Your Memoir
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T153000
UID:6a64c5ecf213992f00c6e867@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this What If writing workshop\, author Sharon A. Crawford u
 ses the 6 senses - taste\, smell\, touch\, sight\, hearing\, intuition\, a
 nd their related emotions to help participants choose the memoir they real
 ly want to write\, then develop it.\nThis workshop combines studying publi
 shed memoir excerpts (including Sharon’s published memoir\,\nThe Enemies
  Within Us\n)\, discussion\, exercises including writing the memoir beginn
 ing\, handouts – workshop outline covering the ABC’s of writing the me
 moir\, research\, using real names or pseudonyms\, etc.​​\nParticipant
 s are encouraged to bring personal photos relating to their memoir to faci
 litate some discussions and exercises.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Richview\, Room A\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a64c5ecf213992f00c6e867
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T153000
UID:6a301aefc7d3cd5800607c04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a series of 6 classes which have be
 en designed to take a learner with no\, or very few skills\, from zero to 
 a solid grounding in the absolute basics. Each class is set up to connect 
 with the previous and next class in a series format.\nDrop-in. No Registra
 tion is required.\nJuly 15\, Class 1: Use the Mouse\nJuly 22\, Class 2: Us
 e the Keyboard\nJuly 29\, Class 3: Use the Web\nAugust 5\, Class 4: Use Go
 ogle Search and Maps\nAugust 12\, Class 5: Use Windows\nAugust 19\, Class 
 6: Use Email - Gmail
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a301aefc7d3cd5800607c04
