BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T153000
UID:69bee67b67801235ed73a990@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Don Mills Library and its neighbourhood is home to a varie
 ty of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry team to explore the n
 atural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differe
 nt species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n
 Free program. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.
 \nRegistration is required.  Please register online.  Registration will 
 open on Monday\, August 10\, 2026.\nPresented as part of TPL’s environme
 ntal program series\, Our Fragile Planet. The series is generously support
 ed by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.\nThe tour will st
 art and end at the\nDon Mills Branch front lobby\nand will be guided by th
 e City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surf
 aces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoo
 r program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable sh
 oes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe incle
 ment weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nIf yo
 u identify as a person with a disability and require an accessibility acco
 mmodation to participate in this program\, please contact Accessibility Se
 rvices by email\, accessibleservices@tpl.ca\, or voicemail\, 416-393-7099\
 , to make a request. Please contact us at least three weeks in advance.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Meeting location: front lobby.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69bee67b67801235ed73a990
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
