UID:6a11b72b8e677a28001e0614@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered why people believe in conspiracies?\nIn
  this book club\, we will be reading books that explore the social conditi
 ons that make people prone to extreme belief.\nThurs. Jun. 11\, 2:00-4:00p
 m\nEscaping the Rabbit Hole\nby Mick West\nThurs. Jul 9\, 2:00-4:00pm\nBla
 ck Pill\nby Elle Reeve\nThurs. Aug. 13\, 2:00-4:00pm\nProject Mind Control
  by John Lisle **BOOK CHANGE**\nThurs. Sept. 10\, 2:00-4:00pm\nConfession
 s of a Media Manipulator\nby Ryan Holiday\nThurs. Oct. 8\, 2:00-4:00pm\nTh
 e Brainwashing of My Dad\nby Jen Senko\nThurs. Nov. 12\, 2:00-4:00pm\nShoc
 k Doctrine\nby Naomi Klein
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Founder's Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a11b72b8e677a28001e0614
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
