SUMMARY:Mount Pleasant Cemetery History (afternoon presentation)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T153000
UID:6a3c22ccfddb082f00fdbd67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Sunnyside Historic Society Presents stories from the crypt
 !\nWhat is the connection between a survivor of the Titanic\, a world clas
 s pianist\, and a prime minister? T\nhey were all buried at Mount Pleasant
  Cemetery.\nJoin us for a combination of story-telling\, pictures\, and sh
 ort skits - on the history of Mount Pleasant Cemetery and the souls burie
 d there.\nNote: This program will run twice on the same day\, from 2-3:30p
 m and 6-7:30pm\, both being the same presentation. Please sign up for a ti
 me that suits you best.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal info
 rmation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the 
 Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information
  will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evalu
 ation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be dir
 ected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3c22ccfddb082f00fdbd67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tech Through the Ages
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T160000
UID:6a4d6c0f1381c628000d37ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on a journey across the technological ages! This progr
 am\, led by professors from Northeastern University’s Toronto campus\, w
 ill open with a look back at technologies of the past\, and then move into
  where we are today with developments like Artificial Intelligence\, befor
 e imagining we are headed in the future.\nAimed at older adults and senior
 s\, this program will be interactive\, with time dedicated to conversation
 \, questions\, and of course\, light refreshments. Northeastern students w
 ill be on hand during the break to answer any tech questions you might hav
 e!\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions abou
 t how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline s
 taff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto O
 N M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium (2nd Floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d6c0f1381c628000d37ad
