BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260820T150000
UID:6a3d6abfc52cdc3600ecd7f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 women and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a fragil
 ity fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Osteopor
 osis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your risk o
 f osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWhat you
  need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fracturing a
  bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical activ
 ity Fall prevention\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8
LOCATION:Mount Pleasant\, Basement program room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d6abfc52cdc3600ecd7f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence? - Part 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T104500
UID:6a3d74f0fddb082f00fdfc1d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how to spot when it is being used\, 
 and considerations when using AI.\nWhat is Artificial Intelligence? Part 1
  - August 15\nWhat is Artificial Intelligence? Part 2 - August 22
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Second Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d74f0fddb082f00fdfc1d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
