BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Movement with the Alzheimer Society of Toronto - Seated Y
 oga with Lisa Brodie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T150000
UID:6a3e8cb06db61d280098257c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an in-person 6-part creative movement series and e
 njoy activating your body in a fun and inclusive space. Each week we will
  stretch\, strengthen and find our flow with Lisa Brodie\, a Certified Yog
 a Teacher and Yoga Therapist. This series is appropriate for learners at a
 ll levels and provides opportunities foreach participant to learn at their
  own pace and in their own style\, from a seated or standing position.\nTh
 is program is presented in collaboration with the\nAlzheimer Society of To
 ronto\n. It is designed for people living with early to mid stage dementia
  or mild cognitive impairment\, or together with a care partner.\nPlease w
 ear comfortable and layered clothing\, sturdy shoes and bring a water bott
 le.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\,  Ground floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cb06db61d280098257c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
